👑🧠 Birbal and the Rich Man’s Pride (Raw Story)

One day, a rich man came to Emperor Akbar.

He said proudly, “I am the richest man in the city!”

He looked down on others and treated them badly.

Akbar asked Birbal to teach him a lesson.

Birbal invited the rich man for a walk.

They reached a large field.

Birbal drew a small circle on the ground and said, “Stand inside this.”

The rich man stood inside the circle.

Birbal asked, “What do you see?”

The man said, “Only the ground around me.”

Then Birbal drew a much bigger circle around him.

“Now what do you see?” he asked.

The man said, “I can see much more.”

Birbal smiled and said, “The bigger your thinking, the more you see. Pride makes your world small.”

The rich man felt ashamed.

💖 Moral:

Pride limits your thinking—stay humble to grow.
